<title>JAPAN: Sanyo to rise nickel-metal hydride battery output.</title>
<headline>Sanyo to rise nickel-metal hydride battery output.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanyo Electric Co Ltd said that it would boost its output of nickel-metal hydride batteries, used for cellular phones and personal computers, by 50 percent to 18 million units a month by the end of calendar 1997.</p>
<p>The increase is planned to cope with increasing demand for nickel-metal hydride batteries, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Sanyo captures an about 30 percent market share on the global market of nickel-metal hydride batteries, she said.</p>
</text>
